the days of Swiss watchmaker sitting out  of the SmartWatch arms race are firmly  behind us Breitling is the latest to  enter the fray with the excess base v55  chronograph the b55 has a beefy 46  millimeter case made from black titanium  and a bright blue rubber strap it looks  like a real aviation tool not a gadget  and borrowed from Breitling's earlier  aerospace line of watches our two little  screens on the dial that let you control  all the extra functions with the crown  and the pushers the big news though is  the app which connects the b55 to your  iPhone  this lets you use your phone to set the  watch control the timers or swap time  zones with ease conversely the watch can  now push its timing data back to the  phone letting you keep track of event  times over the long run and like with  most smartwatches the watch can buzz  when you get a text or have an  appointment coming up the excess base  b55 is available now and is priced at  $8,900 a clear signal that this is meant  to compete with high-end mechanical  watches not whatever the latest devices  from Apple or Motorola it's unclear what  the future of Swiss smartwatches looks  like but for now Breitling's b55 is one  of the more compelling concepts out  there
 

